---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — That Music Therapy Lot | Therapy and Consultation in London"
  description="That Music Therapy Lot are primarily Music Therapists dedicated to making music therapy an option for you — highly-trained specialists in Process-Based Music Therapy and clinical assessment, based in Walthamstow, London, E17. Integrative psychotherapy is available via Therapy With Ben."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="section__eyebrow reveal">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-hero__title reveal">Who we are</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede reveal">
        That Music Therapy Lot are primarily Music Therapists who are dedicated
        to making sure that music therapy is an option for you. We are
        highly-trained specialists based in Walthamstow, London, E17 (Waltham Forest).
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="section section--tight">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="prose reveal">
          <p>
            Our signature is Process-Based Music Therapy — finding a style of
            therapy that resonates with you and your history. Our team are
            highly skilled at identifying patterns and features in your life and
            behaviours that help match the right therapeutic approach.
          </p>

          <h2>We work hard at the start to get the best outcomes at the end.</h2>
          <p>
            All our clinicians maintain registration with the HCPC, good-standing
            CPD records, and a commitment to the standards of proficiency.
          </p>

          <h2>Bucking the trend</h2>
          <p>
            Increasingly, Music Therapists have to exercise more and more
            flexibility to demonstrate their impact. At That Music Therapy Lot,
            we make sure your clinicians have a boat-load of CPD so that they
            can be both flexible and effective.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are also experts in assessment, working to create new and
            innovative assessment tools both in Music Therapy and for wider
            multi-disciplinary teams.
          </p>

          <h2>Meet the founder</h2>
          <h3>Ben Richardson</h3>
          <p>
            Ben started his professional career as a Music Therapist. During his
            early work, he noticed that the major flaw in many clinicians’ work
            wasn’t the therapy — it was the reporting.
          </p>
          <p>
            Inspired by the work of Speech and Language and Occupational
            Therapist colleagues, he began to support a paradigm shift toward
            Process-Based work: targeting measurable verbs rather than objective
            adjectives. That means watching for things like latency, similarity
            in expressions, and variance in responses.
          </p>
          <p>
            Core to Ben’s philosophy is the belief that therapy resistance is a
            myth; it just means the right therapy hasn’t been tried yet. He has
            an excellent track record of engagement with adolescents and young
            adults, often supporting them through an Acceptance and Commitment
            Therapy approach.
          </p>
          <p>
            When working with Ben, you can expect honesty, with what you think
            held in higher regard than what he thinks. He is deeply interested in
            functional truth — the beliefs we hold to be true and act in line
            with — and how these operate as our primary reasons for behaviour.
          </p>
          <p>
            Looking for Ben’s integrative talking therapy practice?
            {' '}<a href="https://therapywithben.uk/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">That’s at Therapy With Ben</a>.
          </p>
          <p>If requested, Ben’s dog Pru can also make an appearance in sessions.</p>

          <h2>Where we’ve helped</h2>
          <ul class="partner-list">
            <li>
              <img
                src="/images/web/Flourish.jpeg"
                alt=""
                width="400"
                height="120"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <div>
                <strong>Flourish Learning Trust</strong>
                <span>Overhauled the clinical referral system.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <img src="/images/web/TCES.png" alt="" width="120" height="120" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <strong>TCES</strong>
                <span>Working to support some of the most disadvantaged young people in London.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <img
                class="partner-list__dark"
                src="/images/web/LimeTrust.png"
                alt=""
                width="200"
                height="80"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <div>
                <strong>Lime Trust</strong>
                <span>Restarted the Music Therapy provision at two schools.</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <img
                src="/images/web/TICE.jpg"
                alt=""
                width="280"
                height="80"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <div>
                <strong>TICE</strong>
                <span>
                  Created a therapeutic music programme which can be delivered
                  digitally for young people in the North East.
                </span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>FAQs</h2>
          <h3>What is Music Therapy?</h3>
          <p>
            Music Therapy is a psychological intervention which uses the musical
            skills of the therapist to support a client’s wellbeing. Find out
            more at the
            {' '}<a href="https://www.bamt.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">British Association for Music Therapy</a>.
          </p>
          <h3>Where do you work?</h3>
          <p>
            Music Therapists can work with anyone and anywhere, but primarily at
            That Music Therapy Lot we work with verbal populations who are
            handling deep-rooted trauma or SEMH difficulties. That being said,
            we are always open to hearing about how we might be able to help —
            so never hesitate to get in touch.
          </p>
          <h3>How do you become a Music Therapist?</h3>
          <p>
            Music Therapists have to train for two years to get an MA in Music
            Therapy from one of eight different teaching courses.
          </p>
          <h3>Where can I find out more?</h3>
          <p>
            You can find out more at
            {' '}<a href="https://www.bamt.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.bamt.org</a>,
            or on
            {' '}<a href="https://www.england.nhs.uk/ahp/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">NHS England’s site about the Allied Health Professions</a>.
            Alternatively, try the
            {' '}<a href="https://www.hcpc-uk.org/standards/standards-of-proficiency/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HCPC’s standards of proficiency</a>
            for a deep-dive into what is expected of us.
          </p>
          <h3>Can anyone be a Music Therapist?</h3>
          <p>
            Music Therapy is a protected title by the Health and Care Professions
            Council. You can be prosecuted for practising Music Therapy without
            being registered with them — don’t worry, we all are at That Music
            Therapy Lot.
          </p>
          <h3>What is Process-Based Music Therapy?</h3>
          <p>
            Process-Based Music Therapy means our clinicians attend to the active
            psychological and musical processes driving change — not just surface
            behaviours or fixed technique playlists — so we can pick the right
            approach for the right moment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="aside-note reveal" aria-label="Founder portrait and registration">
          <figure class="portrait">
            <img
              src="/images/web/BenRichardson.jpg"
              alt="Ben Richardson, Music Therapist and founder of That Music Therapy Lot"
              width="900"
              height="1200"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
          <h3>Registration</h3>
          <p>
            All our clinicians maintain registration to the HCPC, good-standing
            CPD records, and a commitment to the standards of proficiency.
          </p>
          <ul class="trust-list">
            <li><a href="https://www.hcpc-uk.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HCPC</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.bamt.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">BAMT</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://secat.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">SECAT®</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/#contact">Contact us</a>
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
